# Chapter artifacts. Source, findings, per-round histories and run logs ARE tracked;
# anything large or regenerable is not.

# Evolution checkpoints, 12-49 MB each, rewritten every round. A run writes ck_<tag>.npz
# beside its README when launched with ND_OUT=$PWD; the .hist.json sidecar beside it is the
# scientific record and is committed as that experiment's history.json instead.
ck*.npz
ck*.npz.tmp.npz
*_fitness.npz
snapshots/

# `ck_*.npz` used to be the whole rule and it MISSED `ck.npz` -- exp008 runs live in one
# directory per run and name their checkpoint plainly, so six 12 MB files sailed straight
# past it. Hence the wider glob above.
#
# ck.npz.hist.json is a byte-for-byte twin of the run's own steady_state_<tag>.json history
# (save_ckpt writes one, main() writes the other). Track the tagged one, skip the twin.
ck*.npz.hist.json

# Launcher bookkeeping, not results.
DONE

# The two dataset binaries under data/ ARE tracked on purpose (see data/README.md): the .npz
# is the teacher data and actor_s1.pt is force-added so the .npz stays reproducible. Nothing
# else of that kind belongs in here.

# Analytics figures and summaries: regenerate with `python src/analytics/run_all.py`.
src/analytics/out/

# Run logs ARE part of the record here, so undo the repo-wide `*.log` rule. They are a few KB
# each and they are the only place some numbers survive -- the architecture header, the
# held-out line, and the exact failure that ended a run.
!*.log

__pycache__/
